<title>USA: Western Pacific Q3 dil shr loss vs profit.</title>
<headline>Western Pacific Q3 dil shr loss vs profit.</headline>
<dateline>COLORADO SPRINGS, Colo. 1996-10-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			1995</p>
<p> Shr diluted loss	 $0.07   profit	 $0.03</p>
<p> Net	   loss	   910   profit	   372</p>
<p> Revs			45,521		   22,290</p>
<p> Avg shrs		  13,356		   10,644</p>
<p>	  Nine months</p>
<p> Shr diluted loss	 $0.21     loss	 $0.72</p>
<p> Net	   loss	 2,833     loss	 7,484</p>
<p> Revs		     118,540		   29,901</p>
<p> Avg shrs		  13,287		   10,365</p>
<p>(All data 000s except per share.)</p>
<p>NOTES: For nine months 1995, total operating expenses include about $4.8 million of pre-operating and start-up expenses. In accordance with Generally Accepted Accounting Principles, diluted shares outstanding exclude, for periods with a Net Loss, common stock issuable upon stock options granted to employees and directors. Under GAAP, such options are considered anti-dilutive when calculating Loss Per Share. The dilutive effect of these options are included in Earnings Per Share for the three months ended September 30, 1995.</p>
</text>
